This case trains a transformer model for nmoves=1 and individual predictions for each face.

The model used here leverages 2 TransformerEncoders (for N and F) and
concatenates the memory along sequence dimension after adding type embedding.
The model uses a separate DeepONet when the input does NOT contain any history.


"train_3_noise_free.py" uses scaling based on N_left and N_right.
Furthermore, the history_length size is not fixed during training.

FOR NON-PERIODIC BOUNDARIES:
The particle solver and the ML model assume that the first and last cells are
ghost cells, while the DK solver assumes they are valid cells.

DO NOT use "ignore" boundary type in "system_test_mpi_4_batched.py"

The ML model was trained for 2e+6 iterations with the learning rate changing as follows after each 4e+5 iterations.

1. lr = 1e-4, max_lr = 5e-4
2. lr = 5e-5, max_lr = 1e-4
3. lr = 1e-5, max_lr = 5e-5
4. lr = 5e-6, max_lr = 1e-5
5. lr = 1e-6, max_lr = 5e-6 
